      "context": "This is a rare first-person account. Before his awakening, the Buddha ran an experiment on his own mind: he divided the thoughts that arose into two classes, and watched where each class led. What follows is not a rule about which thoughts are forbidden but a report on what repeated thinking does to a mind. The cowherd simile makes the stakes ordinary — a herd kept out of the crops because the cost of wandering is real.",
