      "inference": "The entry point is deliberately mundane, which is the opposite of how meditation is usually sold. The claim is that attention is trainable in the ordinary sense — repeated, unspectacular, cumulative — and that the breath is a suitable first object because it is always present and requires no belief. The sixteen steps continue into feeling, mind, and principles, but this session stops at the body, and that stopping point is a boundary worth respecting.",
