        "inference": "Right livelihood is defined as giving up wrong livelihood, not as finding work you love. But the canon also insists that welfare in this life is real, and that initiative and balance are part of it. The two claims are held together, not ranked by the text.",
        "text": "And what is right livelihood? It's when a noble disciple gives up wrong livelihood and earns a living by right livelihood. This is called right livelihood. \"Byagghapajja, these four things lead to the welfare and happiness of a gentleman in this life. What four? Accomplishment in initiative, protection, good friendship, and balanced finances."
